     0 = max # of 1-4 neighbors
     1 = max # of special neighbors
  special bonds CPU = 0.001 seconds
  read_data CPU = 0.015 seconds
group fq type 1 2
1536 atoms in group fq
pair_style hybrid/overlay lj/cut 10.0 coul/long 10.0 coul/shield/intra 5.0 all
pair_coeff 1 1 lj/cut 0.01275 3.144
pair_coeff 1 2 lj/cut 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff 2 2 lj/cut 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff * * coul/long
pair_coeff * * coul/shield/intra 1.11
kspace_style pppm/samqeq 1.0e-6
if "${start} == npt" then "kspace_modify gewald 0.33957131" "kspace_modify mesh 36 36 36"
kspace_modify gewald 0.33957131
Updated KSpace settings:
  KSpace computation is turned:    ON
  Use MPI collective operations:   OFF
  Use MPI non-blocking operations: OFF
  Gewald manually set to:          0.33957131
kspace_modify mesh 36 36 36
neighbor 2.0 bin
fix chg fq qeq/sam 1 0.0 10.0 ${tol} spcfq_expt.param
fix chg fq qeq/sam 1 0.0 10.0 1.0e-9 spcfq_expt.param
fix_modify chg solver cg nofallback
samqeq: lr solver = CG (symmetric, indefinite-safe)
# npt start: pin the self-term AND the Ewald splitting and mesh that production tuned once at its run start
# (0.37933 belongs to g_ewald 0.33957131 on a 36^3 grid; a fresh run 0 on the NPT box retunes both)
if "${start} == lattice" then "fix_modify chg recip_probes 16" else "fix_modify chg recip_self 0.37933"
fix_modify chg recip_self 0.37933
samqeq: grid reciprocal self-term PINNED at recip_self=0.37933 (raw) = 5.4622 eV/e (not measured; operator is decomposition- and atom-order-independent)
compute dip fq dipole/samqeq
thermo_style custom step pe c_dip
thermo_modify format float %.12g
run 0

